Package: phpvpn
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: VPN client service and command line client
 phpvpn connects this computer to a phpvpn relay and exchanges IPv4 packets
 with the other clients of the same virtual network through a TUN interface.
 .
 The package contains the system service phpvpn-service, started by systemd
 as phpvpn.service, and the command line client phpvpn, which controls the
 service over a local socket and needs neither root nor a graphical session.
 A NetworkManager snippet keeps NetworkManager away from the phpvpn interface.

Package: phpvpn-tray
Architecture: any
Depends: phpvpn (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: tray application of the phpvpn VPN client
 phpvpn-tray shows the connection state of the phpvpn service in the desktop
 notification area and offers Connect, Disconnect, the configuration Wizard,
 the configuration editor, communication contracts, server information and
 statistics.
 .
 The tray starts at every graphical login and never owns the VPN connection:
 closing it or logging out leaves the connection as it is. Without a
 notification area host it shows a control window instead.
